#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147299 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9446e200-ba31-55b4-8c83-b512f45e0c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform of a Function Using Known Laplace Transforms"}] :question/id #uuid "d34aecf1-9491-5cd5-88bc-c276b8df3f77" :question/math-academy-id "e-6653" :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s) = \\dfrac{3}{s^2 + 9}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t} & =\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+{3}^{2}}=\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}} & ={L}^{-1}{L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147300 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a81eb74c-2bdd-58d3-9e9a-8979bdb86dd3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform of a Function Using the Scalar Multiplication Property"}] :question/id #uuid "6887b220-606d-5923-88cb-d13c4606394d" :question/math-academy-id "e-6654" :question/problem "Compute $\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{\\dfrac{7}{s - 9}\\right\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{9t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-9},\\,s>9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by applying the inverse Laplace transform to the above result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{9t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-9} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{{e}^{9t}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-9}} \\\\ {e}^{9t} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-9}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-9}} & ={e}^{9t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the multiplicative property of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7\\cdot {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-9}}=7\\cdot {e}^{9t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{7}{s-9}}=7{e}^{9t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147301 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc8133f2-cbc7-516f-96e6-1bd135fed5a8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform of a Function Using the Addition Property"}] :question/id #uuid "54edc81f-fd2e-5ca8-8779-b3a7a5548e14" :question/math-academy-id "e-6655" :question/problem "Find $\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{F(s)\\right\\}$ for $F(s)=\\dfrac{4e^{-s}-2}{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we decompose the fraction into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4e^{-s}-2}{s} =\\dfrac{4e^{-s}}{s} - \\dfrac{2}{s}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{u}_{1}(t)} & =\\frac{{e}^{-s}}{s},\\,s>0, \\\\ L{1} & =\\frac{1}{s},\\,s>0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $u_1(t)=u(t-1)$ is the unit step function.\n\nTherefore, using the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}-\\frac{2}{s}} & =4{L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-s}}{s}}-2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =4{u}_{1}(t)-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\dfrac{4e^{-s}-2}{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{F(s)\\right\\} = f(t)= 4 u_1(t) - 2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147302 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb4b6a5f-9aed-5dad-9356-4038bf9c0acf" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform Using Partial Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "b7251e69-4dfa-57be-9760-cfc323056148" :question/math-academy-id "e-6656" :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\dfrac{3s}{(s-4)(s+2)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $F(s)$ as a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3s}{(s-4)(s+2)} = \\dfrac{2}{s-4} + \\dfrac{1}{s+2}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{4t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-4},\\,s>4, \\\\ L{{e}^{-2t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+2},\\,s>-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{s-4}+\\frac{1}{s+2}} & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-4}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{4t}+{e}^{-2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\dfrac{3s}{(s-4)(s+2)}$ is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{ F(s) \\right\\} = f(t)=2e^{4t} + e^{-2t}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375772 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9446e200-ba31-55b4-8c83-b512f45e0c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform of a Function Using Known Laplace Transforms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7964c6fa-f9e1-593a-b63b-91d5cfec3927" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375774} {:answer/id #uuid "ca542323-ab02-53eb-82d4-3468434a6f06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375775} {:answer/id #uuid "949b3644-6168-519c-aabe-36e86d2cc8ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375776} {:answer/id #uuid "011980ae-e017-58cb-9490-f3f022e2395c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375777} {:answer/id #uuid "a772f12f-aa38-542e-a9ec-3d93db870aca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7964c6fa-f9e1-593a-b63b-91d5cfec3927" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375774} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9466531-ff06-5bed-98cb-c8e7675ac1bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375773}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0e670e88-2c44-511f-9351-40c005009907" :question/math-academy-id "q-345578" :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{3}{2s-4}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t}} & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-2}=\\frac{3}{2s-4},\\,s>2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t}} & =\\frac{3}{2s-4} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{2s-4}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{2s-4}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{2s-4}} & =\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375779 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9446e200-ba31-55b4-8c83-b512f45e0c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform of a Function Using Known Laplace Transforms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21e0030d-ec59-5e7f-9eaf-735a4efb5a4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375781} {:answer/id #uuid "2448cfbf-9b76-5c65-88e6-644249a908c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375782} {:answer/id #uuid "824e3daa-d5eb-5ee4-aaa4-bde78b9aa999" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375783} {:answer/id #uuid "b5ae7c73-4e65-55b8-a25d-627c324a04b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375784} {:answer/id #uuid "9ad9b9b0-c79d-53dc-a6d4-2861898f683d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "824e3daa-d5eb-5ee4-aaa4-bde78b9aa999" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375783} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ac2f2ea-f1b6-598b-baf2-e4171c4f386b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375780}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "22354821-afe9-5543-8948-39a498baf294" :question/math-academy-id "q-345579" :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{4}{3s+6}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}} & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+2}=\\frac{4}{3s+6},\\,s>-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}} & =\\frac{4}{3s+6} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{3s+6}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{3s+6}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{3s+6}} & =\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375786 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9446e200-ba31-55b4-8c83-b512f45e0c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform of a Function Using Known Laplace Transforms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a4daeed-6b97-5eb6-b3ad-da7a5a862c14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375788} {:answer/id #uuid "31bd77c6-86c5-50a8-ba51-37e67f8723ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{u}_{1}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375789} {:answer/id #uuid "22a07863-5e7e-584c-82c6-5ba3312aeddc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375790} {:answer/id #uuid "b4ae337e-a629-5051-852a-8c6c65015c75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}_{1}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375791} {:answer/id #uuid "4d50a2d2-2bb5-592c-b061-d8a1e5ab7dc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{u}_{1}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d50a2d2-2bb5-592c-b061-d8a1e5ab7dc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{u}_{1}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375792} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7cb8d45-05d5-57d4-8342-d98eae85d75d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375787}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d888eded-dccc-5005-a43d-4bac1f0ea49f" :question/math-academy-id "q-345587" :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{u}_{1}(t)} & =\\frac{{e}^{-s}}{s},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{4{u}_{1}(t)} & =\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{4{u}_{1}(t)}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}} \\\\ 4{u}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}} & =4{u}_{1}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375793 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc8133f2-cbc7-516f-96e6-1bd135fed5a8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform of a Function Using the Addition Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58dbeb80-8913-5555-b0ab-8ea50361dd6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375795} {:answer/id #uuid "181137cd-5675-5e93-b72c-4253ea916d9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375796} {:answer/id #uuid "834082b6-38d6-5380-a05f-cf89f6d4871b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡6t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375797} {:answer/id #uuid "c9270343-c620-54ca-90ab-dcd8a92f08f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375798} {:answer/id #uuid "8ea3ac86-055b-52ef-a5a0-e72483805576" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ea3ac86-055b-52ef-a5a0-e72483805576" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375799} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ca7f46b-1023-5747-94c8-5f1347032322" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375794}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "590cfd05-a2b8-5e45-b8f7-64d1952b203b" :question/math-academy-id "q-345588" :question/problem "Find ${L}^{-1}{F(s)}$ for $F(s)=\\frac{6-5s}{{s}^{2}+9}.$" :question/worked-solution "We decompose the fraction into a sum of partial fractions, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6-5s}{{s}^{2}+9}=\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}+9}-\\frac{5s}{{s}^{2}+9}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t} & =\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9},\\,s>0, \\\\ L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t} & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition and multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}+9}-\\frac{5s}{{s}^{2}+9}} & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}}-5{L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9}} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{6-5s}{{s}^{2}+9}$ is $f(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375800 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a81eb74c-2bdd-58d3-9e9a-8979bdb86dd3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform of a Function Using the Scalar Multiplication Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74d5056b-ff99-53e0-9c06-2a5db0200c58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375802} {:answer/id #uuid "32a24aed-a24c-5dbd-8890-ecf7411b3549" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375803} {:answer/id #uuid "27ba13ba-3156-53b4-b943-0cd2c262bac1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375804} {:answer/id #uuid "1241cf87-a48b-522b-bc74-c2de912d5fdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375805} {:answer/id #uuid "58b25703-3f47-5fa6-8530-11817846330d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375806}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27ba13ba-3156-53b4-b943-0cd2c262bac1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375804} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cf548cc-bdef-55a5-88c9-585ff8faa55c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375801}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d62bb661-1f70-5bd2-a156-a0bc854be402" :question/math-academy-id "q-345606" :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{4}{{s}^{3}}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{2}} & =\\frac{2!}{{s}^{2+1}}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by applying the inverse Laplace transform to the above result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{2}} & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{{t}^{2}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}} \\\\ {t}^{2} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}} & ={t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the multiplicative property of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot {L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}}={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{{s}^{3}}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{{s}^{3}}}=2{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375807 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a81eb74c-2bdd-58d3-9e9a-8979bdb86dd3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform of a Function Using the Scalar Multiplication Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fa7f66f-115b-5637-ae07-2c0d381f73eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375809} {:answer/id #uuid "2ff8fc12-c5b8-51c1-a30e-77df32edefe2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375810} {:answer/id #uuid "4afde3fd-f9da-506d-b245-72ed2a6116d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375811} {:answer/id #uuid "f48b1c8f-eb1a-58e3-aadf-07e823f974a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375812} {:answer/id #uuid "1d72ac8b-d30b-5a13-835c-294d38722ec3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ff8fc12-c5b8-51c1-a30e-77df32edefe2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375810} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b3f7a55-2add-5c4e-b817-fbc34772eaf2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375808}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eed483fc-3e22-55ec-a3a8-5ece7cf8b869" :question/math-academy-id "q-345608" :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=-\\frac{3}{2{s}^{4}}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{3}} & =\\frac{3!}{{s}^{3+1}}=\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by applying the inverse Laplace transform to the above result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{3}} & =\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{{t}^{3}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}}} \\\\ {t}^{3} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}}} & ={t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the multiplicative property of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {L}^{-1}{\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}}}={L}^{-1}{-\\frac{3}{2{s}^{4}}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{-\\frac{3}{2{s}^{4}}}=-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375814 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a81eb74c-2bdd-58d3-9e9a-8979bdb86dd3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform of a Function Using the Scalar Multiplication Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fab1fb5e-b3b1-5adc-8500-a0b6692f7e5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375816} {:answer/id #uuid "826982d4-a82a-5f79-9294-03fa884333ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375817} {:answer/id #uuid "98ff6af8-7d0e-5964-9f79-c498ed17c441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375818} {:answer/id #uuid "fa095400-f791-5c5d-8e55-47251c36bcc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375819} {:answer/id #uuid "52a5996a-3c2b-5d47-a8a7-f244c08fc5aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375820}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98ff6af8-7d0e-5964-9f79-c498ed17c441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375818} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c3698c9-03b4-5de6-ba62-62c524f0f53a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375815}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b5397f8a-96ba-5c5b-8e3e-dff1adb6a98e" :question/math-academy-id "q-345614" :question/problem "${L}^{-1}{\\frac{3s}{4{s}^{2}+16}}=$" :question/worked-solution "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t} & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+{2}^{2}}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by applying the inverse Laplace transform to the above result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t} & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the multiplicative property of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}}=\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{3s}{4{s}^{2}+16}}=\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375821 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb4b6a5f-9aed-5dad-9356-4038bf9c0acf" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform Using Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba7444d4-84a9-5a49-9c57-39a45904d7f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=-{e}^{-4t}+{e}^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375823} {:answer/id #uuid "3a9f6552-9520-55a9-be6a-b2b785c81991" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=4{e}^{t}-5{e}^{-4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375824} {:answer/id #uuid "1fe53b7d-d536-58f3-8069-2b9656899581" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}={e}^{4t}+{e}^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375825} {:answer/id #uuid "795e9efa-bd9c-56dd-9899-fdcfbb17aa92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=-{e}^{4t}+{e}^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375826} {:answer/id #uuid "d0647ae0-be36-53d3-bc35-687953969a08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}={e}^{4t}-{e}^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0647ae0-be36-53d3-bc35-687953969a08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}={e}^{4t}-{e}^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375827} :answer-field/id #uuid "e25ae2c3-3514-51e9-82c2-8edf48d3edb3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e8bbfd15-f611-5044-a87b-e28a975cc360" :question/math-academy-id "q-345623" :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{9}{(s-4)(s+5)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $F(s)$ as a sum of partial fractions, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{(s-4)(s+5)}=\\frac{1}{s-4}-\\frac{1}{s+5}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{4t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-4},\\,s>4 \\\\ L{{e}^{-5t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+5},\\,s>-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition property of the Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-4}-\\frac{1}{s+5}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-4}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+5}} \\\\  & ={e}^{4t}-{e}^{-5t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{9}{(s-4)(s+5)}$ is $f(t)={e}^{4t}-{e}^{-5t}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375828 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a81eb74c-2bdd-58d3-9e9a-8979bdb86dd3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform of a Function Using the Scalar Multiplication Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a639c3b-a7e1-5d53-bca9-d3b660836460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375830} {:answer/id #uuid "467f6005-32dd-587c-8e3b-b240ce184186" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375831} {:answer/id #uuid "08edf7ba-e950-5fda-80fd-6f695bd1829a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375832} {:answer/id #uuid "e68243ff-f960-5981-9eaa-221c35f359f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(t-2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375833} {:answer/id #uuid "147d8777-63e4-502d-bd0e-3caf614f088c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}(t-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08edf7ba-e950-5fda-80fd-6f695bd1829a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375832} :answer-field/id #uuid "48fbdcdb-40c5-53b9-8aa2-0f1948456218" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375829}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c6182ccc-6662-5c68-b032-825b915c52a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-64348" :question/problem "${L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{s-2}}=$" :question/worked-solution "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{2t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-2},\\,s>2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by applying the inverse Laplace transform to the above result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{2t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-2} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{{e}^{2t}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\ {e}^{2t} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} & ={e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the multiplicative property of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}}=4\\cdot {e}^{2t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{s-2}}=4{e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375835 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a81eb74c-2bdd-58d3-9e9a-8979bdb86dd3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform of a Function Using the Scalar Multiplication Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e02f30c4-b7c3-58e6-a3b0-3642b52742e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=2{u}_{8}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375837} {:answer/id #uuid "827a5320-4f12-55b7-adbf-de7927cc15de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=\\frac{1}{8}{u}_{2}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375838} {:answer/id #uuid "aec50ed3-dbc9-5272-b77c-934a17db27af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}={u}_{4}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375839} {:answer/id #uuid "2df8fe55-7363-534e-a4b4-b9e33155678f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=8{u}_{2}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375840} {:answer/id #uuid "2be2f533-9260-5d8e-bc74-8bfdfb9892e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=\\frac{1}{2}{u}_{8}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2df8fe55-7363-534e-a4b4-b9e33155678f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=8{u}_{2}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375840} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e9824be-1f30-58eb-9518-38df261ade30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375836}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d6ccce4-370d-593e-a702-26712d10cb51" :question/math-academy-id "q-64353" :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{8{e}^{-2s}}{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{u}_{2}(t)} & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s},\\,s>0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{2}(t)=u(t-2)$ is the unit step function.\n\nTherefore, by applying the inverse Laplace transform to the above result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{u}_{2}(t)} & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{{u}_{2}(t)}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}} \\\\ {u}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}} & ={u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the multiplicative property of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\cdot {L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}}=8\\cdot {u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{8{e}^{-2s}}{s}}=8{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375842 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc8133f2-cbc7-516f-96e6-1bd135fed5a8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform of a Function Using the Addition Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7936a62-6b09-5fa1-bd97-2c7f4ca8c70a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10{t}^{2}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375844} {:answer/id #uuid "fbffe85b-39c9-5a7e-aad2-fae2e5f8280a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10{t}^{3}+6t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375845} {:answer/id #uuid "cbd47f9b-11bb-5b4c-a238-d98af68b7d13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5t+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375846} {:answer/id #uuid "be7ac788-ae70-5d65-af65-1fc89d0df0cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10t+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375847} {:answer/id #uuid "717d40fe-4ba0-598c-bff9-f73b25e3e6da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{t}^{2}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375848}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "717d40fe-4ba0-598c-bff9-f73b25e3e6da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{t}^{2}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375848} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e741b56-c41d-55e9-abd6-8b6f99c9bb4e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4fb899ba-0e80-5a52-bd7a-c92d37bf5744" :question/math-academy-id "q-64359" :question/problem "Find ${L}^{-1}{F(s)}$ for $F(s)=\\frac{10+3{s}^{2}}{{s}^{3}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We decompose the fraction into a sum of partial fractions, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{10+3{s}^{2}}{{s}^{3}}=\\frac{10}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{3}{s}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{2}} & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}},\\,s>0, \\\\ L{1} & =\\frac{1}{s},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition and multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{10}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{3}{s}} & =5{L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}}+3{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =5{t}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{10+3{s}^{2}}{{s}^{3}}$ is $f(t)=5{t}^{2}+3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148098 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb4b6a5f-9aed-5dad-9356-4038bf9c0acf" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform Using Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94649198-edb3-5008-8a29-c00476a960a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L^{-1}{F(s)} = e^{-2t} - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146600} {:answer/id #uuid "9bbf9abd-1014-5be1-926c-ca0026659632" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L^{-1}{F(s)} = 6e^{t} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146601} {:answer/id #uuid "b9b5daaf-34b0-5358-8310-0f42c6c7b92e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L^{-1}{F(s)} = e^{2t} + 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146602} {:answer/id #uuid "3f53451d-7ab7-50bc-836a-12a5bba80b54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L^{-1}{F(s)} = e^{6t} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146603} {:answer/id #uuid "5d01a5ff-f3f5-5829-b928-5eaa1b02585c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L^{-1}{F(s)} = e^{-t} - 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f53451d-7ab7-50bc-836a-12a5bba80b54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L^{-1}{F(s)} = e^{6t} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146603} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ae6a697-a598-5462-9f9c-da3c43c99d85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146599}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d006ce4c-8de4-5385-bde9-8b9759c49cd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-64381" :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}-6s}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $F(s)$ as a sum of partial fractions, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}-6s}=\\frac{6}{s(s-6)}=\\frac{1}{s-6}-\\frac{1}{s}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{6t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-6},\\,s>6 \\\\ L{1} & =\\frac{1}{s},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition property of the Laplace transform, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-6}-\\frac{1}{s}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-6}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={e}^{6t}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}-6s}$ is $f(t)={e}^{6t}-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148149 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9446e200-ba31-55b4-8c83-b512f45e0c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform of a Function Using Known Laplace Transforms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "893159ef-ba77-59e1-b4c4-375092ba60d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin 5t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146906} {:answer/id #uuid "c6960bbd-bd80-5260-864c-3d8ea76af363" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146907} {:answer/id #uuid "f8e827ed-1d68-589e-888f-3dd95fcf1b9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146908} {:answer/id #uuid "3308d730-6d1b-5d03-84c0-c84f90095291" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t^{5}e^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146909} {:answer/id #uuid "3e98bf9c-e475-51ef-8ce1-f0657d98e231" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos 5t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8e827ed-1d68-589e-888f-3dd95fcf1b9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146908} :answer-field/id #uuid "beec0fe2-3c84-5cba-91c7-0c1c2c99d3bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146905}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e89306dd-1e44-5f34-9936-ddaa75f89781" :question/math-academy-id "q-78055" :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{1}{s-5}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{5t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-5},\\,s>5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{5t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-5} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{{e}^{5t}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-5}} \\\\ {e}^{5t} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-5}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-5}} & ={e}^{5t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375849 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9446e200-ba31-55b4-8c83-b512f45e0c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform of a Function Using Known Laplace Transforms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4027cfe4-ac9a-5143-bb2e-ac69a5e80843" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375851} {:answer/id #uuid "7faf3124-2b0f-56f0-afb0-a06f8035e1e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}_{4}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375852} {:answer/id #uuid "d2cde186-20bf-563d-94f6-837d2104868a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375853} {:answer/id #uuid "b19b91bc-a02b-5afa-bbc9-9cfcee856b8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{u}_{4}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375854} {:answer/id #uuid "1e4abe95-c10a-5357-8241-f27d9828491e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7faf3124-2b0f-56f0-afb0-a06f8035e1e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}_{4}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375852} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0bff623-38c7-5662-a2e1-1c0cdb474e00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375850}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fa14a9bb-ea3d-5cf4-8709-0efce10b7ca3" :question/math-academy-id "q-89811" :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{u}_{4}(t)} & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{u}_{4}(t)} & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{{u}_{4}(t)}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}} \\\\ {u}_{4}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}} & ={u}_{4}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375856 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc8133f2-cbc7-516f-96e6-1bd135fed5a8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform of a Function Using the Addition Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbe6b3f2-6554-55a6-a56c-5ffb161ed890" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375858} {:answer/id #uuid "69c59d25-4b65-5ab9-9ae6-e600cd200de9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375859} {:answer/id #uuid "4ddf7570-48ed-5107-8fab-104db3572df5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+15\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375860} {:answer/id #uuid "f1f6ad08-a9e9-58c5-8e6a-0f99ad75dd25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375861} {:answer/id #uuid "89e990cc-8bd9-5a8e-8570-7b6f8b6ab03e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375862}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69c59d25-4b65-5ab9-9ae6-e600cd200de9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375859} :answer-field/id #uuid "689b5e8a-0ed5-5848-91ee-4e30d034fa8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375857}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7740eec5-a11b-5061-9756-6a98ddeea8b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-89816" :question/problem "Find ${L}^{-1}{F(s)}$ for $F(s)=\\frac{2s+15}{{s}^{2}+9}.$" :question/worked-solution "We decompose the fraction into a sum of partial fractions, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2s+15}{{s}^{2}+9}=\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}+9}+\\frac{15}{{s}^{2}+9}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t} & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9},\\,s>0 \\\\ L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t} & =\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition and multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}+9}+\\frac{15}{{s}^{2}+9}} & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9}}+5{L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{2s+15}{{s}^{2}+9}$ is $f(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375863 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc8133f2-cbc7-516f-96e6-1bd135fed5a8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform of a Function Using the Addition Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3dfdbd7-8a78-5548-903d-4b7ac4835746" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}_{8}(t)+{u}_{5}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375865} {:answer/id #uuid "15f49464-41e0-5715-8d8f-be2104ddb10d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}_{8}(t)+{e}^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375866} {:answer/id #uuid "1af91930-fb86-5e68-b261-3062ee0ac5a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}_{4}(t)+{u}_{5}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375867} {:answer/id #uuid "910364db-07b6-5c00-bb95-fa7d825f1b0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}_{9}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375868} {:answer/id #uuid "5fbc87fa-e9ef-5664-9f28-8ae1f908e121" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t{e}^{8t}+{u}_{5}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3dfdbd7-8a78-5548-903d-4b7ac4835746" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}_{8}(t)+{u}_{5}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375865} :answer-field/id #uuid "07183a77-c804-5a34-8ee5-218d04b24d66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375864}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1a9607cc-f122-593a-bac9-a336dbce5bfa" :question/math-academy-id "q-89818" :question/problem "Find ${L}^{-1}{F(s)}$ for $F(s)=\\frac{2{e}^{-8s}+{e}^{-5s}}{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "We decompose the fraction into a sum of fractions, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{e}^{-8s}+{e}^{-5s}}{s}=\\frac{2{e}^{-8s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{u}_{8}(t)} & =\\frac{{e}^{-8s}}{s},\\,s>0 \\\\ L{{u}_{5}(t)} & =\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s},\\,s>0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{5}(t)=u(t-5)$ and ${u}_{8}(t)=u(t-8)$ are the unit step functions.\n\nTherefore, using the addition and multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{2{e}^{-8s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}} & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-8s}}{s}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}} \\\\  & =2{u}_{8}(t)+{u}_{5}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{2{e}^{-8s}+{e}^{-5s}}{s}$ is $f(t)=2{u}_{8}(t)+{u}_{5}(t).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375870 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc8133f2-cbc7-516f-96e6-1bd135fed5a8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform of a Function Using the Addition Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fd36a50-56c0-516c-849b-cb9a7bd9f7ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-24{e}^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375872} {:answer/id #uuid "e85a2192-579c-55d8-b24b-d503865e0577" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8t-{t}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375873} {:answer/id #uuid "b53a61b6-466f-5aec-8bf8-bfb2698b8c03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-8{t}^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375874} {:answer/id #uuid "eaa5a13a-3439-50a1-b1af-e3bf13c2acb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t-6{t}^{2}{e}^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375875} {:answer/id #uuid "b3a0ef70-0369-59b9-8bbc-8b00f29b8cb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{t}^{2}-{t}^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375876}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e85a2192-579c-55d8-b24b-d503865e0577" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8t-{t}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375873} :answer-field/id #uuid "304875b3-0039-58c3-b610-42baa092756d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375871}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ab2c0b19-e441-5d4b-912c-e8299ee580ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-89820" :question/problem "Find ${L}^{-1}{F(s)}$ for $F(s)=\\frac{8{s}^{3}-24}{{s}^{5}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We decompose the fraction into a sum of partial fractions, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8{s}^{3}-24}{{s}^{5}}=\\frac{8}{{s}^{2}}-\\frac{24}{{s}^{5}}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{t} & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}},\\,s>0, \\\\ L{{t}^{4}} & =\\frac{24}{{s}^{5}},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition and multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{8}{{s}^{2}}-\\frac{24}{{s}^{5}}} & =8{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{24}{{s}^{5}}} \\\\  & =8t-{t}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{8{s}^{3}-24}{{s}^{5}}$ is $f(t)=8t-{t}^{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375877 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb4b6a5f-9aed-5dad-9356-4038bf9c0acf" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform Using Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf239e99-b16a-5eb1-9580-8400877cd9b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=2{e}^{2t}+3{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375879} {:answer/id #uuid "eb56e667-8d50-5aff-a8f0-148f0cab145a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375880} {:answer/id #uuid "52957234-b54d-5e52-8eaf-cbd070aa240e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=10{t}^{2}+{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375881} {:answer/id #uuid "b81cdbfb-fffe-506d-897d-036d4628ca66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=2{e}^{2t}-2{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375882} {:answer/id #uuid "0f2f2313-849b-5152-876d-5f9a4a934e91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b81cdbfb-fffe-506d-897d-036d4628ca66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=2{e}^{2t}-2{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375882} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f1ba755-d966-5f19-812a-8fa9e2542266" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375878}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c32439a8-2f0a-52f2-ba4c-04ee07df7da8" :question/math-academy-id "q-89821" :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{10}{(s-2)(s+3)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $F(s)$ as a sum of partial fractions, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\frac{10}{(s-2)(s+3)}=\\frac{2}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s+3}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{2t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-2},\\,s>2 \\\\ L{{e}^{-3t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+3},\\,s>-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition property of the Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s+3}} & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}}-2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}-2{e}^{-3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{10}{(s-2)(s+3)}$ is $f(t)=2{e}^{2t}-2{e}^{-3t}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375884 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb4b6a5f-9aed-5dad-9356-4038bf9c0acf" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform Using Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64c766d8-4b41-5b55-91c6-dfd9fc095c01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{9t}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-9t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375886} {:answer/id #uuid "4eb08989-f226-524c-aacc-4afd55db7d81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=1-{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375887} {:answer/id #uuid "e22b7ac3-df5d-5851-b586-85a5c78bc48f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=\\frac{1}{6}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{6}{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375888} {:answer/id #uuid "d39c2be3-e6e4-52b9-a886-7b755abbe118" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}={e}^{3t}-{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375889} {:answer/id #uuid "52458cc7-3050-5d9a-88d0-0b78ac7d1d41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e22b7ac3-df5d-5851-b586-85a5c78bc48f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=\\frac{1}{6}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{6}{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375888} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a4a4972-524f-5441-a339-4220201ef38b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4eaf773d-1394-5e6f-85c6-d4046ea05b5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-89824" :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}-9}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $F(s)$ as a sum of partial fractions, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}-9}=\\frac{1}{(s-3)(s+3)}=\\frac{1}{6(s-3)}-\\frac{1}{6(s+3)}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{3t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-3},\\,s>3 \\\\ L{{e}^{-3t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+3},\\,s>-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition property of the Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{6(s-3)}-\\frac{1}{6(s+3)}} & =\\frac{1}{6}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-3}}-\\frac{1}{6}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{6}{e}^{-3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}-9}$ is $f(t)=\\frac{1}{6}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{6}{e}^{-3t}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375891 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb4b6a5f-9aed-5dad-9356-4038bf9c0acf" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform Using Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5425feea-1e6c-5d83-a4f9-1fe0a5d1c681" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375893} {:answer/id #uuid "42883f00-6d11-5c5b-be38-b23599c5e8e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375894} {:answer/id #uuid "d16f580f-a38b-5632-8f37-8df34a676989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=1-5t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375895} {:answer/id #uuid "f25c7f6e-ef3a-5ae1-a878-2b6dc356b470" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=1-{e}^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375896} {:answer/id #uuid "3c3dc4dc-faa3-58ad-9c4f-ff4331d1fed4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=t+{t}^{2}{e}^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f25c7f6e-ef3a-5ae1-a878-2b6dc356b470" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=1-{e}^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375896} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e2b3a95-b8eb-56af-a75e-3686864588a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "94214f15-a4b1-50b9-9005-990ab0ea5ce5" :question/math-academy-id "q-89826" :question/problem "Find ${L}^{-1}{F(s)}$ for $F(s)=\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}+5s}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $F(s)$ as a sum of partial fractions, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}+5s}=\\frac{5}{s(s+5)}=\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{1}{s+5}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{1} & =\\frac{1}{s},\\,s>0 \\\\ L{{e}^{-5t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+5},\\,s>-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition property of the Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{1}{s+5}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+5}} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-5t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}+5s}$ is $f(t)=1-{e}^{-5t}.$"}]}
